  "notes": "Toronto big-room rap: hard drums plus melodic hooks. The distinguishing parameter is loudness rather than density — `velocityTiers` is lifted across the board (accents 112–127, mains 88–102) for the \"almost pop-level transient\" the research describes on the layered kick and snare, while the hat stream stays an ordinary trap 16th with tight 32nd fills. Percussion accents are hooks in their own right, so congas, rim and timbale are authored on the offbeat rather than left to the genre's default rim/snap pair. The melody splits its register wide (67–96) with the highest `octaveJumpProb` in this batch outside DJ Khaled, which is what a flute-or-choir lead over a bell counter sounds like on one part. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ INFERRED: the `velocityTiers` numbers. The research says \"almost pop-level transient\" qualitatively and names no figures; the ratios are mine.",
